              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Every fleet owner eventually faces this question: should you buy OEM or aftermarket semi truck parts?",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At first glance, OEM (original equipment manufacturer) parts might seem like the safer choice. After all, they're made by the same manufacturer as your truck. But today's aftermarket parts industry has come a long way, offering dependable quality, competitive pricing, and greater availability than ever before.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For drivers whose business depends on their trucks, the goal isn't just to find a part that fits; it's to find a part that lasts. That's where Sun State International steps in: helping you make smart, reliable choices that keep your truck and your bottom line moving forward.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-what-are-aftermarket",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What Are Aftermarket Semi Truck Parts?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "what-are-aftermarket"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-are-aftermarket-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Aftermarket parts are built by third-party manufacturers, not the original truck maker, but they're designed to meet or even exceed OEM standards. They're used for everything from brake components and filters to engine parts and body replacements.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-are-aftermarket-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At Sun State International, our parts team carefully vets the aftermarket suppliers we carry, ensuring that every part meets the durability and safety standards you expect. When we recommend an aftermarket option, it's because we'd trust it in our own trucks.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-benefits",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The Benefits of Aftermarket Parts",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "benefits"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-benefits-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For many owner-operators and fleet managers, aftermarket parts make solid business sense. Here's why:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-benefits-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "1. Lower Cost, Same Fit",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-benefits-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Aftermarket semi truck parts are generally less expensive than OEM parts, making them an attractive choice when you're managing tight margins or maintaining multiple vehicles. Lower cost doesn't have to mean lower quality, especially when you work with a reputable dealer like Sun State International.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-benefits-4",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "2. Wider Availability",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-benefits-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "While OEM parts can sometimes take weeks to arrive, aftermarket options are typically in stock and ready to go. This faster turnaround means less downtime and fewer delays on the road, critical for drivers with delivery deadlines and service commitments.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-benefits-6",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "3. Comparable Performance",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-benefits-7",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Many aftermarket parts perform just as well as OEM counterparts. In fact, some are even enhanced to address known weaknesses in original designs. The key is choosing parts from trusted brands and certified dealerships, not from unverified online sellers.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-when-oem",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When OEM Still Makes Sense",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "when-oem"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-when-oem-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "That said, OEM parts still have their place, particularly when your truck is under warranty or you're repairing major components like the engine, transmission, or emissions system. OEM parts are guaranteed to match the manufacturer's exact specifications, which can be essential for maintaining warranty coverage or long-term resale value.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-when-oem-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At Sun State International, we supply both OEM and high-quality aftermarket parts, helping you make the best decision for your truck's age, mileage, and workload.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-at-a-glance",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "OEM vs Aftermarket Parts at a Glance",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "at-a-glance"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "compare-at-a-glance-1",
                  "type": "compare-table",
                  "props": {
                    "headA": "Feature",
                    "headB": "OEM Parts",
                    "headC": "Aftermarket Parts",
                    "rows": [
                      {
                        "a": "Manufacturer",
                        "b": "Made by the original truck manufacturer (e.g., International®)",
                        "c": "Made by third-party manufacturers to fit OEM specifications"
                      },
                      {
                        "a": "Cost",
                        "b": "Higher price point",
                        "c": "Typically 20–40% less expensive"
                      },
                      {
                        "a": "Availability",
                        "b": "May require special order or longer lead times",
                        "c": "Widely available, often in stock"
                      },
                      {
                        "a": "Warranty Coverage",
                        "b": "Guaranteed fit and may be required for warranty repairs",
                        "c": "Some brands offer warranties, but not always linked to factory coverage"
                      },
                      {
                        "a": "Quality & Performance",
                        "b": "Guaranteed to match original design and specs",
                        "c": "Quality varies by manufacturer; top-tier brands often equal or exceed OEM"
                      },
                      {
                        "a": "Best For",
                        "b": "New trucks, warranty repairs, or critical systems",
                        "c": "Older trucks, budget-conscious maintenance, or non-critical replacements"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
